    "details": "The OpenSSL poject reports:\n\n> - Heap Buffer Overflow in CMS Key Unwrapping (CVE-2026-63072)\n>   (Moderate)\n> - Invalid Pointer Dereference in CMP Server via Crafted protectionAlg\n>   (CVE-2026-63076) (Moderate)\n> - RPK Server Signature Algorithm Selection Can Dereference a Missing\n>   Certificate (CVE-2026-14457) (Low)\n> - Excessive Memory Use Buffering DTLS Records for a Future Epoch\n>   (CVE-2026-54874) (Low)\n> - Untrusted Sender DN Used as Format String in CMP Response Validation\n>   (CVE-2026-63073) (Low)\n> - CMP Indefinite Cache Growth of ExtraCerts (CVE-2026-63074) (Low)\n> - QUIC ACK-only Packet Retention Can Cause Memory Exhaustion\n>   (CVE-2026-63075) (Low)\n> - AEAD Forgeries with Empty Ciphertext When Using EVP_Cipher()\n>   (CVE-2026-75803) (Low)\n",
